fix: key per-source limits on the source Caddy verified (#62)
Behind the single public origin the API's socket peer is Caddy, so `request.socket.remoteAddress` gave the entire internet one ADR-0025 budget — a per-source control acting as a global cap that one crawler could exhaust for everyone.

## What changed

**The API half.** `apps/backend/src/api/verified-source.ts` reads the address Caddy verified from `X-Verified-Source`, but only after a constant-time comparison of `X-Proxy-Authorization` against a shared deployment secret — so forwarded context is accepted across the private boundary from Caddy and from nowhere else. Context that is absent, unauthenticated, chained, or not a single address fails closed with HTTP 403 per `docs/threat-model.md:73`, rather than falling back to the proxy's own address. Naively trusting `X-Forwarded-For` was rejected for the reason the issue gives: a caller could vary it per request and mint a fresh budget every time.

The limiter still keys on a salted hash, so no source address is retained.

**The Caddy half.** `deploy/caddy/Caddyfile` trusts no upstream proxy, deletes every inbound forwarding header (including the two it uses itself), and sets verified context on the `/graphql` proxy. It validates against Caddy 2 (`caddy validate`). The global browser-security headers stay with #53.

**Configuration.** `API_TRUSTED_PROXY_SECRET` (min 32 chars) is required in production. Without it the API keys on the connection itself, which is what local development and the Playwright suite need — so #61's raised test limit keeps working unchanged.

## Two things the review caught

- Liveness and readiness are probed over private networking, never through Caddy, so the first version would have answered 403 to every probe and the deployment could never have gone healthy — with ADR-0038 verifying the API before Caddy exists at all. Those two routes now key on the connection they arrive on.
- Refusals are counted against that connection too, so an origin presenting nothing cannot buy an unbounded path through the API or an unbounded run of log lines.

## Verification

Seven tests at the real HTTP server plus `parseAppConfig`: two verified sources get independent budgets; forwarded context from an untrusted caller is refused; missing, chained, and non-address context fails closed; IPv6 works; refusals stay bounded; health probes answer; direct connections still key on the socket.

`pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, 45 unit, 68 component, 141 integration, and 9 Playwright journeys all pass.

The deployment evidence the issue asks for (`docs/security-verification.md:79`) is a release-gate activity; that document's Caddy row already names trusted-proxy behaviour, so no new row was added. `docs/adr/0058-authenticate-forwarded-source-context.md` records the decision and ADR-0028 links forward to it.

Closes #62

